\title{bsfa: Bayesian Stochastic Frontier Analysis}
\description{
Markov chain Monte Carlo methods for the Bayesian estimation of stochastic frontier models. The package implements Gibbs samplers with data augmentation for composed-error frontier models in the tradition of van den Broeck, Koop, Osiewalski and Steel (1994), supporting half-normal and exponential inefficiency, production and cost frontiers, and cross-sectional as well as time-invariant panel specifications. Posterior distributions of observation-specific efficiency scores are obtained directly from the augmented draws rather than from point predictors.
}
